../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:196:- **Icons on buttons (2026-10-24):** primary and secondary buttons carry an icon only when it helps the user recognise the action at a glance — calling, scheduling, viewing, skipping, direction (→ next). No icon when the label must be read: confirming, finalising, releasing, and answers to a question. Quiet buttons never have icons. One icon per button, from `icons.js`, before the label (direction arrows after). **Scope:** labelled buttons only — header icons, the close ×, status and notice icons are not buttons and are not covered; adding time ("Add time" with a plus) counts as scheduling.
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:202:- **Button icon size steps with the button size** (Apurva, 2026-11-02; replaces the D-81 F27 pair-only rule): **56px action buttons (18px label) → 20px icon; 48px compact buttons (16px label) → 16px icon.** Icons stay on the icon scale (16 / 20 / 24) — like type and spacing, each size is a step on a fixed scale, never an in-between value; the icon is one step at or just above its label (as in Carbon, Atlassian and Fluent). **Icon-only buttons** (Back, Help, notifications, Profile, close ×, viewer controls) are not labelled buttons and keep a **20px** icon. Set centrally in `components.css` by button size (`.tm-btn--lg` → 20, compact → 16, `.tm-btn--icon` → 20), overriding any size in the markup; screens never size button icons. SALT's code copy states no per-button icon size; this is a Truemeds addition (`beyond-salt.md`).
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:221:| Header | Title 20/28 semibold, left · ✕ right (48px target, glyph on the 16 margin — the same as the compact task header, B-07) · **no divider**. Optional one-line subtitle (L3). |
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:228:- **Quiet text for "stay" (D-81 F11):** the option that keeps things as they are ("Stay signed in", "Keep available") is quiet text (`tm-btn--quiet`), never a secondary button.
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:230:### 9.5 Feedback
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:234:| **Notice** | Neutral / warning / error (L5); stays until the cause is gone. **Warning** when something blocks the main action or runs on a timer (offline, locks, near expiry); **error** when an action failed; **neutral** only for side information (D-54). Text wraps balanced (A-22). **Placement (A-19, Round 4 item 2, 2026-11-02):** a notice that is the **result of an action** sits next to the control that did it — on a screen with a pinned bar, inside the bar above its button, in the band style of §3 (Home "ending soon", setup / add / request failures, the offer's "Couldn't turn on…", the case and calling bar notices); on a screen without a bar, 16 below the field it came from (D-98) or 8 below the button (A-14). A notice about **the bar's own action** — the result of the last tap, or why its button is disabled now (offline, "No cases right now") — is also in the bar. A notice about the **screen's general situation** (unlock "isn't available", Home idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stays at the top of the panel, not tied to a button (lane-request 7, Round 4). **Alignment (D-86, 2026-11-03):** the band inside the bar is centred (icon and text as a group, wrapped lines centred, balanced breaks kept); every other notice (top of page, inside sheets, in content) stays left-aligned. |
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:238:| **Rule** | One message per cause — never field error + notice + toast for the same thing. |
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:240:**Keyboard (D-81):** when a text field is focused, the field scrolls above the keyboard with its label and helper visible (so the doctor can see what they type into). The pinned action bar hides while the keyboard is open and returns when it closes (same reason as §8 point 9, 16px clearance). Applies to Prescribe and the case page.
../../../../../design-system/RULES.md:246:- Sentence case for buttons, titles, labels and sheet titles. No full stop on titles; full stops on sentences in notices and helpers.
