../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:35:- After sending, server results show as a notice: not registered (with the sign-up route), offline, couldn't send, too many attempts (button counts down "Try again in m:ss"), account inactive (button becomes **Call Doctor Ops**).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:36:- When the "Try again in m:ss" countdown ends, the "Too many attempts" notice goes away and **Send OTP** works again (D-98).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:40:- The terms line stays during **Verifying…** and **Checking…**, so Verify & sign in never moves (D-81 F5, amends D-44 for those two states). The cooldown line reads "Checking…" alone, with no "Didn’t receive it?", and the boxes stay focused (D-81 F7).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:43:- Wrong code: digits stay visible with red borders; the first new keystroke replaces the whole code. The message is "Wrong code."; from 2 tries left it counts ("Wrong code. 2 tries left."), and at 1 try left it uses the singular ("Wrong code. 1 try left.") (D-81 F1; no next-step wording, D-53 pt 2).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:48:- **Sign-in on a locked number** goes straight to OTP in the locked state (`otp_locked`): code field and Verify off, the lock time and "call Doctor Ops" shown, Change still available (D-81 F6).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:51:**Faster sign-in** (D-45, D-47)
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:52:- Offered on its own screen after an OTP sign-in on a phone that supports it, while faster sign-in is off: after the first sign-in, then again at each later OTP sign-in until it is turned on, at most 3 times (setting `fasterOfferMax`, D-104; "not available" counts as shown). The footer is the action bar (Round 4, item 1); the content above it scrolls. Subtitle on one line: "Use your screen lock instead of an OTP." (A-06). **Turn on** → phone prompt → Home. **Cancelled** prompt → back to the offer, no message. **Failed** → stays on the offer; "Couldn't turn on faster sign-in." sits in the bar above Try again (A-19) · Try again · Not now (D-61, D-65). **Offline** → "You're offline. Check your connection." (D-66). **Unavailable** (the phone answers "unavailable" at Turn on) → stays on the offer, unchanged (title, subtitle, tile and the three points): the amber warning notice "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." sits in the bar (same slot as Offline and "Couldn't turn on", A-19), the primary reads **Continue** → Home and Not now is hidden; not enabled, recorded as offered, can be turned on later in Profile (D-93, state `offer_unavailable`). **Not now** → Home; offered again at the next OTP sign-in, up to `fasterOfferMax` times in total (D-104); can be turned on or off in Profile (D-69).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:54:- Returning unlock: two buttons (D-105), **Unlock** (primary) · **Use OTP instead** (quiet); no "Switch account". The phone's own prompt; 3 failed tries `[MOCK]` → the same as Use OTP instead. **Use OTP instead** opens **Sign-in with the remembered number filled in** (cursor at the end, Send OTP ready); no SMS is sent until the doctor taps Send OTP. To change account, the doctor edits the number there. This Sign-in follows the normal Sign-in rules: no Back; the phone's back gesture leaves the app (D-101); reopening the app shows unlock again. The footer is the action bar (Round 4, item 1); the content above it scrolls. If unavailable: "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." is a standing state, so the neutral notice stays at the top of the panel; **Use OTP instead** is the main button in the bar (A-19) and opens the same prefilled Sign-in.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:59:## 3. Home and availability `[LOCKED]` (D-36, D-40, D-47, D-53)
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:60:- **While Setting… or Adding…** the wheel, the duration chips, Cancel and × are disabled (D-81 F9).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:61:- **Set availability** stays pinned to the bottom of the screen in every state, with or without a notice (D-81 F12, D-43), **inside the action bar** (Round 4, 2026-11-02, item 1). The content above the bar scrolls on short phones (at 360×640 the timer and the wheel are never clipped); the bar never covers the last content; toasts sit above the bar.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:62:- **Time added:** 5:00 + 30 min shows 35:00 (D-81 F10).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:63:- **End availability** is greyed out while offline; the offline notice explains (D-81 F13).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:64:- **Log out confirm:** "Stay signed in" is quiet text, like "Keep available" (D-81 F11, RULES §9.4).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:74:- **Result notices on Home** ("Availability ends soon", setup / add / request failures) sit inside the action bar, above its button (RULES §9.5, A-19). "No cases right now" and offline are the bar's own action, so they sit inside the bar above the button (lane-request 7). Screen-wide standing notices (idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stay at the top of the panel.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:76:- **No cases:** neutral notice "No cases right now. Try again in a minute." Auto re-check `[OPEN OQ-019]`.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:93:| Calling — the whole call (`call.calling` 2 / 7a, `call.calling-transfer` 11) | End-of-call script in the slot under Order details, above the medicines, from the tap (D-58 pt 18) | Status line "Calling {name}…" (D-74) **only — no Callback on a live call** (CW-A1, D-83). No separate Connecting / On call states (D-58 pt 14). **No End call** — the doctor ends the call on the phone | Header Back hidden from the tap on Call patient / Call again (D-80, D-81 F21); phone back → toast "Finish this case first. Then you can go back to Home." (`a-back-blocked`) |
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:95:| Call not valid (`call.ended-early` 6, `call.result-missing` 7d) | No script — the call has ended (D-58 pt 24) | 6: notice · **Call again** · Callback (no Unavailable, D-58 pt 23) · 7d (Cat4): notice · **Confirm prescription** · Callback + Unavailable (reason sheet, D-75) · 7d (Pilot): **Confirm & forward** · Callback + Unavailable, no Skip HA (CW-D2) | Blocked |
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:99:**Empty case (D-80 pt 4, D-81 F23; D-83 CW-A6, K4):** no **Call patient**. An amber notice at the top of the panel says "No medicines on this order. Our Ops team will check it." (D-84; was "This order has no medicines. Release it — our Ops team will check it.") (where the released case goes is open, OQ-035). The main button is **Release case**, which releases directly (Releasing…, no sheet) and returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). Header Back does the same. When Order details is hidden, View Rx is left-aligned (B-16).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:100:**Call ended, outcome card (D-81 F26, retired D-83):** the "End the call to get your next case." warning is retired with state 15b; after the hang-up the card is title only, neutral (MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85; `call.forwardedAfterHangup` retired, §14).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:101:**Bar and card rules (Round 4, 2026-11-02):** a bar notice that is the result of an action ("Couldn't confirm…", "Prescribe or disable…") sits inside the action bar above its button (RULES §9.5, A-19). Cards on the case page and Prescribe are 16 apart; the end-of-call script card has 16 padding below in every state (B-03, B-04, B-05). The callback-scheduled card uses the calendar icon and the patient-unavailable card the phone-off icon, the same icons as their buttons (B-22). A two-line patient name makes the header taller, not tighter (B-06). Long medicine titles wrap balanced (B-13).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:103:**Leaving a case:** the back-blocked toast breaks between its two sentences (B-21). An **attempted call** = leg 2 answered (the patient picked up) (D-58). Once a call is attempted, leaving is blocked until the case is closed (callback, unavailable, confirm). Before that, header **Back** opens the "Leave this case?" sheet — **Release case** (the case returns to the queue) or **Stay** (D-58 point 20, OQ-024; label D-84 CA-22; on Ready and states 3 and 4 only). Header Back is on 1, 3 and 4 only, while the patient has never been reached. It is hidden from the **Call patient** / **Call again** tap, incl. Calling 7a, the 7b question, Transfer, and the callback sheets, and never returns once the patient answered, also on a later 3 / 4 (D-80 pt 1, D-81 F21). Behind the leave sheet, Releasing… and Release failed the screen is **Ready** (D-81 F22). The backend refuses Release once our call request is accepted, unless the result is 3 or 4 (D-80). Release returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). If the patient answered just before the tap, the backend refuses the release and the doctor stays on the case (`a-release-failed`, "Couldn't release this case. You're still on it."). The unassign action itself is a backend dependency (OQ-024). Help stays available at every stage and is the way to reach Doctor Ops when something keeps failing. App closed or phone off mid-case → reopening goes straight back into the case `[OPEN OQ-025, backend]`.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:137:| 2 | `call.calling` | Calling (whole call) = 7a | Doctor taps Call; until a result | "Calling {name}…" status line only · no Callback (CW-A1) · no header Back (D-81 F21) | `t02-calling` / `s7a-calling` |
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:138:| 3 | `call.not-through` | Didn't go through | Request refused, or leg-1 network/vendor error | Red notice · Call again · header Back | `t03-not-through` |
