../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:165:Retired: `b-missed-call`, `b-didnt-connect` (sheets) — replaced by the automatic close and the notices. `a-leave-sheet` / `s7e-leave-sheet` is the approved Release sheet (D-58 point 20). The old state name **hold** for "didn't connect" is retired (old Flag 4).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:176:- **Confirming… / Transferring… (D-81 F24–F25):** medicine rows and notes are read-only and muted, with no arrows. View Rx stays the outlined button (D-76).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:192:- **Transfer vs forward** (D-57): transfer = the patient is handed to an HA on the same call; forward = an HA calls the patient back separately. A failed transfer goes as a forward; after Transferring (13) the doctor sees state 15 `call.transfer-failed` (CW-E1: the transfer couldn't start) — amber card "Forwarded to Health Advisor" with "Read the script, then end the call." (`call.transferFailed`) + script `call.forwardedTell` (§5, D-58 pts 17, 21, 23; MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85). No separate "HA didn't join" notice (D-58 pt 8 replaced by pts 15–17); the render id `t15-ha-no-join` is only a file name. A forward (15, B3) is confirmed only on the partner's result (CW-F2).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:193:- Confirm: button shows "Confirming…", everything else disabled, no second submit. Failure: notice in the bar "Couldn't confirm. Nothing was lost." (D-65). **Unclear result** (no answer from the server): the button stays on "Confirming…" — the same screen as `a-confirm-busy` — while the app checks; then it shows the confirmed card or the failure notice, never a second submit (D-69). An unclear result is checked before retrying (no double confirm).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:197:✅ **Flag 5 — answered (Apurva, 2026-10-16):** Confirm is blocked while any medicine is Pending. The button stays tappable; on tap a notice in the bar says "Prescribe or disable {n} medicines first." and the page scrolls to the first Pending medicine. Applies to all three confirm buttons; Callback, Skip HA and Unavailable stay allowed. *Original flag:* The old code lets the doctor confirm while some medicines are still Pending (not prescribed, not disabled). No decision covers this. Options: (a) block Confirm until every medicine is Prescribed or Disabled, with a note saying how many are left; (b) allow it, and Pending medicines are dropped from the prescription; (c) allow it with a confirmation sheet. Recommendation: (a) — a prescription with unreviewed medicines is a clinical risk.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:206:- **Confirm callback** closes the case (status card "Callback today at 3:00 PM"). The case goes to the callback pool, not back to this doctor (D-36) `[MOCK: the app treats it as closed for this session]`. Save failure: notice in the sheet, choices kept.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:242:- **Rx failed notice:** 16 below the header, as elsewhere (B-19).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:246:- **Food (optional):** After food · Before food · Empty stomach (tap again to clear). **Additional instructions (optional)**, with the helper "Printed on the prescription." (D-81 F19).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:248:- **An error on Prescribe scrolls the screen to the first error.** The M / A / N "choose a dose" error is field text under the grid, not a tinted box; other errors sit under their field (D-81 F16).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:250:- **A disabled medicine** opens with the note "Disabled: {reason}. Prescribing it will enable it again." (state `d-disabled`, D-81 F17, D-20).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:254:**Printed line** = schedule · duration · food (if chosen) · instructions (if written), e.g. "1-0-1 + SOS 1 tablet (max 1 tablet/day) · 6 months · After food". **SOS limit (D-80 pt 3, D-81 F14):** the daily total in the medicine's unit: "2 puffs as needed (max 8 puffs/day)"; a total of 1 is singular ("max 1 tablet/day"); cream prints "Apply as needed (max 3 times/day)".
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:259:- **Keyboard rule (D-81):** on Prescribe (Other dose, Additional instructions) and the case page (Chief complaints, Doctor notes) the focused field scrolls into view above the keyboard with its label and helper. The pinned action bar hides while the keyboard is open and returns when it closes (same reason as D-43).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:264:- **View Rx** opens the customer's prescription full screen: zoom (50–400%), rotate, reset, pinch and drag. Load failure: notice + Try again; ✕ always closes. Disabled while confirming.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:270:- **Loading** (case): a skeleton shaped like the loaded page: an Order details row, Medicines and Notes blocks, in the same places (D-81 F28).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:273:Follow `docs/feedback-state-map.md` exactly. Summary for the case page: loading = card outlines, no actions · load failed = notice + Try again · offline = yellow notice in the bar "You're offline. Reconnect to call or confirm." (D-54) · an action tried offline fails with one error notice, nothing lost · release failed = notice, doctor stays on the case.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:281:- **Profile earnings (D-81 F10):** **₹20 per confirmed prescription** (Apurva, 2026-11-02), so 3 prescriptions today show Earned ₹60.00 · Incentive ₹0.00 (0 while setting availability). The app shows what the backend sends; earnings count once a case is confirmed (D-73). Incentive rules are not defined yet (₹0.00 in the prototype).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:322:Not yet approved; Apurva reviews the before/after sheets. Standing decisions (D-42 to D-81) are unchanged; where a line above was edited for Round 4 the edited line governs. Rules live in `design-system/RULES.md` §3, §8, §9.5; the audit is `docs/renders/2026-11-01-fix-round/CONSISTENCY-AUDIT.md`.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:326:**Notice placement (A-19, item 2).** A notice that is the **result of an action** sits inside the bar, above its button (Home "Availability ends soon", setup / add / request failures, the offer's "Couldn't turn on…" and "isn't available" (D-93), the case and calling bar notices). A notice about the **bar's own action** (offline, "No cases right now", the results above) sits inside the bar. A notice about the **screen's general situation** (unlock "isn't available", Home idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stays at the top of the panel (lane-request 7). On a screen without a bar, a result notice sits 8 below the field or button it came from (A-14).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:328:**Bar notice band (item 3).** A bar notice is an edge-to-edge band on the bar's top edge: full tint, 1px bottom edge in its tone, same icon and text. Page-content notices keep their box.
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:336:**Gaps and cards.** Cards that stack are 16 apart on the case page, Prescribe and Profile (B-05, A-13, B-04). Notices and their controls: 8 (A-14).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:340:**Back and calling (unchanged).** Back is hidden from the Call tap on, as in D-81 F21; the leave sheet, Releasing… and Release failed sit over Ready (F22).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:342:**Copy (messages.json).** "Use your screen lock instead of an OTP." (A-06). The three OTP messages with "Doctor Ops" and a time keep the phrase on one line (A-17). Balanced notice wrap is set centrally (A-22, B-20).
../../../ui-screens/app-logic.md:361:- **Release → Home.** Empty case: amber notice at the top of the panel, **Release case** releases directly, no sheet (CW-A5, CW-A6).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:99:- **Rejected:** "Tablet · Prescribe" subtitle; a coloured form tag (colour is only for status); full-width Disable
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:178:- **Sheets:** one template everywhere — title + grey cross (close) on the right, no drag handle; optional grey subtitle;
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:180:  "Select reason" subtitle. Customer-unavailable sheet uses the same template (no big icon).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:184:- **Closed states:** after Unavailable, Callback or a completed action, the card shows one plain notice
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:310:- **Screen:** Apurva's layout as is. Logo, "Welcome, Doctor.", subtitle "Your partner in thoughtful, affordable care.", Mobile number (+91), helper "We'll send you a verification code by SMS.", **Send OTP**, footer
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:313:  not 6–9). Problems after sending show a notice in the same spot and leave the field neutral: not registered
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:320:- **Build:** built 2026-10-12 on the draft branch (D-38); merges to `main` with the Home screens.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:383:### D-38 · Sign-in, OTP and returning unlock built into the prototype — 2026-10-12
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:400:- **Known differences from the handoff:** notice icons use the shared icon set instead of the ⓘ / ⚠ text glyphs;
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:401:  sign-in notices are larger than OTP notices, as in the approved renders (worth unifying later).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:418:- Keep the quick presets, 15-minute minimum and 15-minute increments. Show “Minimum 15 minutes” once on setup; no repeated reminder on the add-time sheet.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:425:- Two error structures: field error and action notice; existing warning/status/success/loading patterns remain distinct semantic feedback. Preserve D-39 timing and D-40 wheel selection.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:432:  - **Task header** — Back + screen title, **no logo**. (2026-10-14: Back only where there is a previous screen — none on the faster sign-in offer or returning unlock, D-47; the case page's Back follows D-48; hero vs compact size, D-49.) Used on **OTP**, the **faster sign-in offer**, **returning unlock**, the **case page** and every other step or task screen.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:452:  - **Notice:** directly under the boxes. **Resend line** under the notice, one centred line: while waiting "Didn't receive it? **Resend in 0:30**" (timer slightly heavier, fixed-width digits, not tappable); when available "Didn't receive it? **Resend code**" (brand link, 44pt tap area).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:455:  - **Locked:** keyboard closes, boxes disabled, warning notice carries the countdown and "call Doctor Ops", Verify shown disabled so nothing jumps when the lock ends. No resend line, no consent line.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:459:- **Changes:** D-38 "keyboard closes … on the 4th code digit" and "faster-sign-in card … ticked" are replaced. `concepts/2026-10-09-otp-screen-spec.md` is historical for layout. D-34, D-35, D-39 unchanged.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:464:  - Not now → Home. Offered again later (when: OQ-023) and always available in Profile. No Back on this screen; the phone's back gesture = Not now (D-47).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:466:- **Why:** it can't go unnoticed, so it drives adoption (the point is cutting SMS OTP cost); a pre-ticked or easy-to-miss checkbox on OTP risks a sneaky opt-in; the phone's prompt makes sense right after a deliberate "Turn on". It also declutters OTP.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:468:- **Changes:** replaces the OTP opt-in in D-38 and the OTP spec. D-32's original "offered once after the first OTP sign-in" idea is effectively restored, as a native screen.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:484:- **Changes:** D-43 helper and notice sizes superseded by L4 and L5 (14/20). D-44 slot sizing superseded by L1.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:486:### D-47 · Phases A–C final review decisions — 2026-10-14
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:494:  - **Returning unlock (B):** **no Back** — it's the first screen when the app opens; "Not you? Switch account" leads to sign-in. Title is the greeting "Hello, Dr. Apurva". Unavailable notice: "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." (no repeat of the "Use OTP instead" button).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:496:    - Bug: helper text ("Minimum 15 minutes") must never be clipped or hidden under a notice; content scrolls. The guard checks for clipped text.
