../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:977:### D-96 · Native hand-off kit for the React Native team, piloted on Sign-in — 2026-11-09
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:978:- **Decision (Apurva):** the React Native team gets a **hand-off kit** in the repo (`handoff/`), not a token list or hand-written RN code. For people: foundation files (tokens, icons, messages, native fonts), a spec for each building block (parts × states → native token), a screen viewer (tap an element → block, tokens, spacing; "tokens used" table; raw values flagged red), behaviour links and a "what changed" list. For their AI: `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md`, a skill, one data file per screen, and `DECIDED.md` / `OPEN.md`. Everything factual is generated from files we already maintain. (1) The app team builds and owns the RN components and screens; we own the contract. (2) The October TSX and hand-off notes in `ui-screens/native/` are marked "don't use — see `handoff/`" once the kit is approved (backlog). (3) Pilot screen: Sign-in. Proposal: `docs/proposals/2026-11-09-native-handoff-kit.md` (§6 is the done-checklist). **Amended same day (Apurva):** built the D-95 fast-build way: Codex writes the checks from the proposal before the build and is the fresh-AI tester and the critic; tap-to-inspect at 390 only (360 as pictures); one evidence sheet; runs in parallel with the prototype build (own files only). (Numbered D-96: D-95 is the fast build.)
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:988:- **Decision (Apurva):** the desktop preview frame is **390 : 844** (exactly 390 × 844 when the window allows, scaled down evenly otherwise), replacing 9:16 in the central design system (`design-system/RULES.md` §7, all projects). Review controls sit in **one column on the right**, top-aligned with the frame. "Test on phone" becomes the first folding row of the review panel (it was a separate card in the left gutter, session 4). Also: the QR / play link uses the Mac's network address when served locally, the default story is the happy path (patient answers, call over the gate), panel summaries wrap instead of being cut off, the **test numbers and codes** (app-logic §11) are listed in the Sign-in answers row (tap to fill), and "Settings" becomes **"Timings and limits"** in plain words with a Rule / Stand-in tag, moved with Event log under "Advanced" at the bottom.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:992:### D-98 · Hand-off kit review: missing tokens added, countdown end, small rulings — 2026-11-09
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:993:- **Decision (Apurva):** (1) Sizes the Sign-in kit found with no token become design-system tokens (border width, focus ring width and offset, logo lockup width, icon sizes incl. the notice icon 20, spinner size and ring), listed in `beyond-salt.md` as `[PROPOSED]`; the "+91" prefix and the logo's accessible name "truemeds for doctors" become `messages.json` keys used through `MSG()`. No visual change. (2) When the "Try again in m:ss" countdown on Sign-in ends, the "Too many attempts" notice goes away and Send OTP works again (closes kit OPEN o06; app-logic §2).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:994:- **Main thread rulings (bugs, fixed where they occur):** red in the kit means only a typed size, colour or word (layout keywords and zeros are shown, not flagged); the kit excludes the reference page's own review and capture scaffolding (H05); the notice sits 16 below the field as the approved pictures show, and RULES §8.3 wording is corrected; the busy spinner ring uses `--tm-content-inverse` instead of `#fff` (same white); RULES §8.13's stale "Sign-in is 174 today" line is removed; the native logo ships as PNG exports of the locked SVG (no redraw); the static font files from the font's upstream repository at the commit Google Fonts pins are accepted.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1002:- **Why:** the hand-off kit (D-98) found typed sizes; the audit found ~150 more. Root cause: RULES §2 only covered colour, spacing, radius and shadow (SALT's families), so typed sizes passed every review, and no one asked what native needs when `native/tokens.ts` was created (2026-10-30). Fixing before Home, Case and Prescribe are built avoids building them with typed values and redoing them.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1003:- **Rejected:** fixing after the build (rework); a "constants file" per app (D-98); a 2–3 hour run (the token table was settled in the main thread, so the run only applies it).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1010:### D-101 · Hand-off kit Product answers for Sign-in (o04–o26) — 2026-11-09
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1011:- **Decision (Apurva, on the main thread's recommendations):** (o04) more than 10 digits that aren't a +91 / 0 prefix → show "That’s more than 10 digits. Check the number." instead of cutting silently. (o05) no passive offline notice on Sign-in; the notice shows only after Send OTP. (o07) the logo's 16 from the top is measured from the **safe area** (below the status bar / notch). (o08) Android back on Sign-in (the first screen) **leaves the app**. (o10) coming back from OTP via Change keeps the number and it edits normally (the first typed digit does **not** replace it). (o11) Terms → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/terms-and-conditions`, Privacy → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/privacy-policy` (placeholders, linked from the live Terms page), configurable from the server, not typed into the app. (o17) Sign up opens a browser **inside the app** (with a close button). (o18) nothing is remembered per number; an earlier answer shows again only after a new Send OTP. (o25) "New to Truemeds? Sign up" becomes one copy entry with a `{link}` placeholder. (o26) "Call Doctor Ops" on a device that can't call → open WhatsApp to the same number; without WhatsApp, show the number with a copy button.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1026:### D-104 · Faster sign-in offer: again at each OTP sign-in, at most 3 times — 2026-11-10
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1027:- **Decision (Apurva):** after "Not now" (or the phone's back gesture), the faster sign-in offer comes back at the doctor's next OTP sign-in, and the next, until faster sign-in is turned on — **at most 3 times in total** (a Product setting, starting value 3). After that it isn't shown again; Profile still turns it on. "Not available on this phone" counts as shown. Remembered per phone and mobile number, as today. Closes OQ-023; replaces D-45's "offered once".
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1028:- **Why:** the point is cutting SMS cost, and every OTP sign-in is an SMS sent — the right moment to ask again. Doctors stay signed in between sessions, so OTP sign-ins are rare and the re-ask isn't frequent; the cap stops nagging a doctor who has decided no.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1031:### D-105 · Returning unlock: two buttons; Use OTP opens sign-in with the number filled in — 2026-11-10
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1032:- **Decision (Apurva):** returning unlock drops "Not you? Switch account". It keeps **Unlock** (primary) and **Use OTP instead** (quiet). Use OTP instead, and the automatic fallback after 3 failed unlocks, open **Sign-in with the remembered number filled in** — no SMS until the doctor taps Send OTP. To change account, the doctor edits the number there. Sign-in reached this way follows the normal Sign-in rules: no Back button; the phone's back gesture leaves the app (D-101); reopening the app shows unlock again. Amends D-61 point 3.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1033:- **Why:** three stacked buttons with two quiet ones looked odd; Switch account and Use OTP instead both led to sign-in, so one control now does both. Not sending the SMS straight away also avoids an SMS when the doctor only wanted to switch account.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1034:- **Rejected:** keeping Switch account; a special back gesture from this Sign-in to unlock (rare mistake; reopening the app already returns to unlock; one Sign-in behaving differently is harder to build and explain).
