### 9.4 Bottom sheets — one template
| Part | Rule |
|---|---|
| Background | Page dimmed behind the sheet (`.tm-overlay`). |
| Top | Rounded top corners; **no drag handle** (the ✕ is always there). |
| Header | Title 20/28 semibold, left · ✕ right (48px target, glyph on the 16 margin — the same as the compact task header, B-07) · **no divider**. Optional one-line subtitle (L3). |
| Spacing | 16px side margins (`--tm-space-page`, same as screens) · 16px header → content · 24px + safe area at the bottom. |
| Content | Fields, chips, or **option rows** (one shared style for reason lists: title + one-line description, full width, 48px+; tapping applies). Labels inside a sheet ("Select reason", "Date", "Time") use `.tm-sheet__label` — one style, 8 above the field (B-14, 2026-11-02). |
| Actions | §9.1 order and size (56px, full width). **Pinned (Round 6, 2026-11-02):** the actions are the sheet's last part and stay on screen when the content is taller than the space — the content scrolls between the pinned header and the pinned actions. The hairline and soft upward shadow show only while content scrolls under them (`design-system/src/sheet-scroll.js` sets `.is-stuck`; screens with sheets load it). Sheet buttons stay fully visible and tappable at 390×844 and 360×640. Reason lists need no button. **Confirmation sheet** ("Leave this case?", "Discard changes?"): the action the sheet asks about on top — red outline if it can't easily be undone, primary otherwise — and the "stay" option as quiet text below. A sheet offering two real actions (e.g. Retry call / Mark as unavailable) is a choice, not a confirmation (D-54). |
| Closing | ✕, tap outside or swipe down = cancel — **except while an action is in progress**. Unsaved input asks before closing. |
| Size | Up to 85% of the screen height; the content scrolls, header and actions stay pinned. Max width 640px on desktop. |
| Over the bar | **A sheet always covers the pinned action bar of the screen behind it (Round 6, 2026-11-02).** The scrim and the sheet sit above the bar in every state: no part of the bar shows or takes a tap while a sheet is open. |
- **Quiet text for "stay" (D-81 F11):** the option that keeps things as they are ("Stay signed in", "Keep available") is quiet text (`tm-btn--quiet`), never a secondary button.
.tm-overlay { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgb(0 0 0 / calc(var(--tm-overlay-default) * 1%)); z-index: var(--tm-layer-overlay); }   /* raw-ok: scrim is black at the overlay-token opacity (SALT has no black semantic colour) */
/* Round 6 (RULES §9.4): the sheet is the one scroller. Its header and its actions are pinned (sticky) at the top and bottom
   edges, so the sheet's own buttons stay visible and tappable when the content is taller than the space.
   Z-order: the sheet (layer-sheet 901) and its scrim (layer-overlay 900) sit above the pinned action bar (layer-sticky 10) in every screen, so a sheet always covers the bar. */
.tm-sheet {
  position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: var(--tm-layer-sheet);
  background: var(--tm-surface-primary);
  border-radius: var(--tm-radius-2xl) var(--tm-radius-2xl) 0 0;
  /* RULES §9.4 — one template: no drag handle, page margin at the sides (16, D-67). The top and bottom spacing sit in the pinned header and actions. */
  padding: 0 var(--tm-space-page);
  max-height: var(--tm-sheet-max-height); overflow: auto;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column;
}
.tm-sheet:not(:has(> .tm-sheet__actions)) { padding-bottom: calc(var(--tm-space-xl) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }
.tm-sheet__header { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: var(--tm-layer-raised); flex: none; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--tm-space-md); min-height: calc(var(--tm-target-min) + var(--tm-space-lg)); padding-top: var(--tm-space-lg); background: var(--tm-surface-primary); border-radius: var(--tm-radius-2xl) var(--tm-radius-2xl) 0 0; }
.tm-sheet__title { margin: 0; font-size: var(--tm-font-size-title-sm); line-height: var(--tm-font-lineheight-lg); font-weight: var(--tm-font-weight-semibold); color: var(--tm-content-primary); }
.tm-sheet__subtitle { margin: var(--tm-space-xs) 0 0; font-size: var(--tm-font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--tm-font-lineheight-sm); color: var(--tm-content-secondary); }
.tm-sheet__close { margin-right: calc((var(--tm-icon-size-md) - var(--tm-target-min)) / 2); }   /* .tm-btn.tm-btn--quiet.tm-btn--icon, 48px; glyph sits on the 16 margin, same as the compact header (B-07, 2026-11-02) */
/* B-14 (2026-11-02): one sheet-label style — the field-label style, 8 above the field (RULES §8.3). Used for "Select reason", "Date", "Time". */
.tm-sheet__label { display: block; margin: 0 0 var(--tm-space-sm); font-size: var(--tm-font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--tm-font-lineheight-sm); font-weight: var(--tm-font-weight-semibold); color: var(--tm-content-primary); }
.tm-sheet__body { margin-top: var(--tm-space-lg); flex: none; overflow: auto; }   /* own block formatting context, as before (the sheet scrolls, not the body) */
